.IR danbylab (2),
.IR danbylabtest (1)
.SH BUGS
This is a steady state, not an event.  T is the fraction of a continuous
beam that gets through, and nothing here is a particle arriving, pausing
and emerging.  The question of how LONG tunnelling takes is not answered
here and is not settled in the literature either.
.PP
The barrier is one-dimensional and perfectly rectangular.  Alpha decay
is really a Coulomb barrier, curved, and the exponential there is an
integral through the forbidden region rather than a single ka.
.PP
At E exactly equal to V both the numerator and sinh squared vanish
together, and the true limit is finite.  Rather than special-case it the
spec adds 1e\-6 to |E\-V|, so the value at exactly the barrier top is
wrong in the sixth decimal.  It is one point of an axis that is swept,
and no slider can land the sweep on it exactly.
.PP
.IR Danbylabtest (1)
checks T + R = 1 at four hundred energies, the resonance identity at
three widths and three orders, T against its closed form on both sides
of the barrier, that a zero height or a zero width transmits everything,
and that a real barrier does not.  The closed-form check is the one that
matters most: the resonance identity is exact BECAUSE the sine vanishes
there, so it cannot see the V squared factor at all, and breaking V
squared to V passes it.  Only the off-resonance comparison catches that.
